Ah thanks! I agree. Took a stab at merging them on GitHub:
https://tlswg.org/tls13-pkcs1/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1.html
https://author-tools.ietf.org/api/iddiff?doc_1=3Ddraft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1=
&url_2=3Dhttps://tlswg.github.io/tls13-pkcs1/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1.txt

Look reasonable? I can cut another draft with the changes.

On Thu, Sep 25, 2025 at 3:14=E2=80=AFPM Paul Wouters <paul.wouters=3D
40aiven.io@dmarc.ietf.org> wrote:

> Hi,
>
> In general the document looks fine but I do find the Introduction and
> Security Considerations to have a lot of overlap in what they talk about.
>
> I think that could be consolidated by moving and merging all but the last
> paragraph of the Security Considerations to Section 1, and leave the
> Security Considerations to talk about security considerations _when
> implementing this draft_ (I personally prefer the more detailed text in t=
he
> Security Considerations over the Section 1 text describing the same issue=
s
> but I'm fine with whatever works)
>
> Paul
